  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0AM6">Definition <span data-tag="0AM6">87.31.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $f : Y \to X$ be a morphism of formal algebraic spaces over $S$. We say $f$ is <em>proper</em> if $f$ is representable by algebraic spaces and is proper in the sense of Bootstrap, Definition <a href="/tag/03XZ" data-tag="03XZ">80.4.1</a>. </p>
